  body: |
    # Transitional addition for the source’s ESA conversion

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source’s transitional addition protects the conversion amount for a qualifying existing award and is explicitly distinguished from other earlier transitional additions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 45600–45602 describe conversion-specific protection, reduction and termination, including the stated 5 April 2020 end boundary. This does not establish an ongoing 2026 payment or UC transitional protection.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 45600, PDF page 48](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=48)
    - [DMG 45601, PDF page 48](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=48)
    - [DMG 45602, PDF page 48](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6717a7f6194d62fb6854056b/dmg-chapter-45-ib-sda-and-is-claims-and-reassessment.pdf#page=48)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:29.299489Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

