  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/esa-legacy-conversion
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source limits this transitional addition to converting existing awards and gives a termination boundary.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol8-ch45/0048
      quote: "45600 The TA is an amount which ensures that no claimant entitled to an existing award will be entitled\nto less benefit where their award qualifies for conversion to ESA. In this Chapter the abbreviation TA only\nrefers to a TA for the purposes of converting an existing award to ESA. Some claimants are already\nentitled to a TA as part of their existing award of IS, which was awarded when their Supp B award was\nconverted to IS. Other claimants have transitional protection when their award of SB or IVB was treated\nas a transitional award of IBLT. These amounts are taken into account when calculating the TA on\nconversion of an existing award to ESA, and then terminated when the existing award is converted to\nESA. See DMG 45204 for guidance on the meaning of an existing award."
      locator: DMG 45600
    - page: page/dmg-vol8-ch45/0048
      quote: "45602 The TA is gradually reduced, for example on uprating or when the conditions for a dependency\nincrease are no longer satisfied. Any entitlement to TA is terminated when entitlement to a converted\naward ends, or on 5.4.20 if it is still in payment immediately before that date. See DMG 45800 et seq for\nfurther guidance."
      locator: DMG 45602
